  "worked_solution": "We are given the units $\\frac{\\text{cm}}{\\text{day}},$ and we want to convert this into $\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{year}}.$ We're converting two units instead of just one, so we're going to have to multiply by two conversion factors:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{cm}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{year}}\n$$\n\nOne of the conversion factors should change $\\text{cm}$ to $\\text{m}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{cm}}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{cm}}}\\cdot \\,\\frac{?}{?}=\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{year}}\n$$\n\nThe other conversion factor should change $\\text{day}$ into $\\text{year}.$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{cm}}}{\\cancel{\\text{day}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{cm}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{days}}}{\\text{year}}=\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{year}}\n$$\n\nSo, our conversion formula is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{cm}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{cm}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{days}}{\\text{year}}=\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{year}}.\n$$\n\nNow that we have our conversion formula, we need to determine the correct numbers to use, and apply it.\n\n- The rate given in the problem statement is $2\\,\\frac{\\text{cm}}{\\text{day}}.$\n\n- There are $100$ centimeters in one meter, therefore, there are $\\frac{1}{100}$ meters in one centimeter.\n\n- There are $365$ days in one year.\n\nApplying our conversion formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\,\\frac{\\text{cm}}{\\text{day}} & =2\\,\\frac{\\text{cm}}{\\text{day}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{100}\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{cm}}\\cdot 365\\,\\frac{\\text{days}}{\\text{year}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{100}\\cdot 365(\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{cm}}}{\\cancel{\\text{day}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\cancel{\\text{cm}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\cancel{\\text{days}}}{\\text{year}}) \\\\  & =7.3\\,\\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{year}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $2$ centimeters per day is equivalent to $7.3$ meters per year. In one year, the tree grows by $7.3$ meters.",
